# Maintain Cursor-Docs-Changelog.md

Whenever you change documentation, config, Michu tooling, dashboards, scripts, or CI on GitLab `cursor-test`, add a row to `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-Changelog.md` in the same task.

## Routing (Area column)

| Change location | Area |
| :-------------- | :--- |
| `user-guide/` | User Guide |
| `admin-guide/` except `Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` | Admin Guide |
| `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` or docs-as-code workflow | Docs-as-code workflow |
| `config/` | Config (NAC) |
| `michu/` | Michu |
| `trundle/` | Trundle |
| `scripts/`, `package.json`, pipelines, `AGENTS.md`, dashboard runbooks | ADO tooling and dashboards |

## Entry format

Add or extend the table under `## DD-MM-YYYY` (UK date format; newest date sections first):

```markdown
## DD-MM-YYYY

| Area | What changed | Link | sync_id | sync_repo | request_form_ids | michu | Why |
| :--- | :----------- | :--- | :------ | :-------- | :--------------- | :---- | :-- |
| User Guide | Brief description | `user-guide/Page.md` | pending | gitlab | admin-initiated | - | Optional one-line reason |
```

## Required behavior

1. Add a new `## DD-MM-YYYY` section above older dates, or append rows to the same-day table when part of the same publish batch. Keep date sections newest-first.
2. Always write **`pending`** in the `sync_id` column - CI backfills the GitLab hash.
3. Set **`sync_repo`** to `gitlab` for all changes in that repository.
4. Set **`michu`** to `yes` only for rows from a Michu doc-drift merge request; otherwise `-`.
5. One row per logical change; include **Link** as a relative path to the primary file or doc.
6. Do not edit the ADO mirror for changelog rows - ADO is read-only and overwritten by the mirror.
7. If no meaningful change occurred, state that no changelog update is required.

For Paragon Knowledge / ParaDOCS plugin doc changes in the plugin repo, add rows to the Changelog section of `docs/ParaDOCS-Plugin-Overview.md` or `docs/Paragon-Knowledge-MCP-Overview.md` (by product). See `changelog-ownership.mdc` for the full multi-repo map and anti-duplication rules.
